      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Independently of materiality, the driver's trailing-90-day record is clean and cannot support a pattern finding: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 812 — a ratio of 0.00, far below the 0.05 ratio threshold POL-RD-06 sets and far below its alternative 3-flag trigger. No repeat-deviation pattern is established on these figures, so none of the POL-RD-06(a), (b) or (c) effects can fire against this driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The quantum is capped by the POL-RD-02 arithmetic, which the fare_breakdown has already computed: recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 21.0 km + 0.28 x 26.0 min) x 1.0 (the surge_multiplier read from the FARE_BREAKDOWN, not the trip_record) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP/surcharge/waiting - 0 promo = 27.63; refund = 35.64 charged_total - 27.63 = 8.01, rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05 = 8.05. That is $1.95 short of the $10.00 the rider claims, so the claim is overstated and the largest payable figure this record supports is 8.05.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00101", "EV-TRIP-00101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing can be added on top of that POL-RD-02 figure. This trip carries no ERP gantries and no tolls — erp_gantries is empty and both the on-optimal-route and off-optimal-route ERP totals are 0.00 — and it carries no airport surcharge, the trip neither originating nor ending at an airport, so airport_surcharge is 0.00. POL-RD-09 therefore has no pass-through correction to make, and the total sum the rider can recover on this record is the 8.05 POL-RD-02 refund and no more.",
