  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 8.05,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver — this is a route-deviation case on trip TRP-00101, and both advocates actually converge on the same figures, which I accept.\n\nIs the deviation established? Yes. The platform's GPS trace (EV-GPS-00101) records 27.18 km against the booked optimal of 21.0 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-00101) — an excess of 6.18 km, or 29.4%. Both of POL-RD-01's establishment gates pass (excess above 20% of optimal, and above 0.8 km absolute). The trace figure governs over the rounded trip-record copy of 27.2 km, as POL-RD-01 requires; nothing turns on the 0.02 km rounding. The trace is clean for POL-RD-07 purposes — 229 fixes, no gaps, max_gap 0.0 s, 10-second sampling — so no independent corroboration is needed to prove the excess, and the driver's own chat message MSG-00101-002 ('sorry boss missed the exit, coming back now') and his submitted statement confirm the navigation error anyway.\n\nDoes anything excuse it? No. There is no traffic advisory in the bundle (EV-ADVIS-00101-01 is empty), so POL-RD-03 cannot run. The rider requested no waypoint — every waypoint_hint is null and her message only objects to the route — so POL-RD-04 is unavailable. No endpoint was amended (POL-RD-05) and this is not a pooled trip (vehicle_type RYDE_X, solo_optimal null), so POL-RD-12 does not apply.\n\nHow much? The fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-02 governs and the number is arithmetic, not discretionary. Reading the surge multiplier from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier (1.0): recomputed fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 21.0 km + 0.28 x 26.0 min) x 1.0 + 0.80 platform fee = 27.63. Refund = 35.64 charged_total - 27.63 = 8.01, rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05 = 8.05. That is above the SGD 0.50 de-minimis floor but only 22.5% of charged_total, well under the 90% full-refund share, so the ruling is PARTIAL_REFUND of 8.05, not the $10.00 the rider estimated by hand. There is no ERP, toll or surcharge line to add on top (erp_gantries empty, tolls 0.00, no airport surcharge), so POL-RD-09 makes no separate correction and nothing is double-counted. Driver compensation does not arise: the rider was billed 27.2 km against a 27.18 km trace, so there is no unbilled-distance shortfall under POL-RD-04.\n\nThe materiality point both advocates raise is accepted: at 29.4% and 6.18 km this excess falls below BOTH of POL-RD-01's materiality thresholds (50% and 8.0 km), so it is not a MATERIAL deviation, the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is not triggered, and no driver-conduct referral follows. Independently, the driver's trailing-90-day record shows 0 deviation flags across 812 completed trips (ratio 0.00), so no repeat pattern could be established even if the check had been required. No clause in the policy produces a referral on these facts, so the referrals list is empty.\n\nAmount moved: 8.05 SGD to the rider. The present charge of 35.64 does not stand in full; 27.63 of it does."
