    "explanation": "Both parties largely agree on the facts, and the record decides the case. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00101) measures 27.18 km driven between the recorded pickup (10:21:05) and dropoff, against the booked optimal of 21.0 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-00101). The excess is 6.18 km — 29.4% of optimal — which clears both of POL-RD-01's establishment gates (more than 20% of optimal and more than 0.8 km absolute), so the route deviation is ESTABLISHED. It does not clear the materiality gates (more than 50% of optimal, or more than 8.0 km), so this is not a MATERIAL deviation: the POL-RD-06 driver-conduct check is not engaged and no conduct referral arises; in any event the driver's trailing-90-day record (deviation_flags_90d 0 over 812 completed trips, EV-DPROF-00101) shows no pattern. The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 (229 fixes, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0, 10-second sampling), so the deviation stands on the trace alone; the driver's chat message MSG-00101-002 ('sorry boss missed the exit, coming back now') and his counterparty statement independently concede the navigation error. No exoneration applies: the only advisory artifact (EV-ADVIS-00101-01) carries no payload, so POL-RD-03 cannot run; the chat contains no waypoint request from the rider and every waypoint_hint is null, so POL-RD-04 is undecidable and unavailable; there is no amendment under POL-RD-05 (amended_optimal_distance_km is null) and this is not a pooled trip under POL-RD-12 (RYDE_X). On the fare, the model is METERED, so POL-RD-02 governs: recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 21.0 km + 0.28 x 26.0 min) x 1.0 surge (read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee = 26.83 + 0.80 = 27.63. Refund = 35.64 charged_total - 27.63 = 8.01, rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05 = 8.05. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor, so money moves, and at 22.5% of charged_total it is far below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is a PARTIAL_REFUND of 8.05 — not the $10.00 difference the rider estimated by hand, which was never traceable to the fare lines. Nothing is added under POL-RD-09: the ERP arrays are empty, tolls_erp is 0.00 and airport_surcharge is 0.00, so there is no pass-through line to correct or to double-count. No driver compensation arises: the billed distance (27.2 km) is not less than the trace distance, so POL-RD-04's compensation limb does not fire. This leaves the charge of 35.64 standing as to the balance (27.59) and refunds 8.05 to the rider.",
